"Runs DeltaBlue on fructus, which can't load the benchmark by its name like
 Harness and Run do. The argument is the number of inner iterations,
 default 1.

 THESE ARE CUT-DOWN RUNS: ARE-WE-FAST-YET RUNS DELTABLUE WITH 12000 INNER
 ITERATIONS, AND ON FRUCTUS IT CAN HAVE AT MOST 1538, SINCE THE PROJECTION
 TEST COMPUTES i * 10 + 1000 IN 15 BITS. SO ITS RESULTS DON'T COMPARE WITH
 FULL RUNS."
RunDeltaBlue = (
    run: args = (
        | innerIterations |
        innerIterations := args length > 1
            ifTrue: [ (args at: 2) asInteger ]
            ifFalse: [ 1 ].
        (DeltaBlue new innerBenchmarkLoop: innerIterations)
            ifTrue: [ 'DeltaBlue (CUT DOWN, NOT AWFY SIZE): ok' println ]
            ifFalse: [
                'DeltaBlue (CUT DOWN, NOT AWFY SIZE): incorrect result' println.
                system exit: 1 ]
    )
)
